 paper's own wording.","citation_ids":["cite.step.construction_weighted_not_cover"],"evidence_ids":[],"id":"step.construction_weighted_not_cover","kind":"claim","label":"A weighted support with no divisor cover","locator":"Proof of Proposition 5.1, p. 11","source_id":"paper.short.pdf","statement":"With pairwise disjoint finite sets $P_k$ of odd primes such that $2^k/4\\le S_k<2^k/4+1$ and $E=\\bigcup_{k\\ge1}\\{2^kd:d\\mid M_k\\}$, the weighted sum for $P=\\{2\\}$ is finite, while $\\mathbb E_{F_m}\\log^+f_{F_m}\\ge\\frac{m-1}{8}\\log2$. Thus $E\\notin\\mathcal C$.","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/nodes/step.construction_weighted_not_cover","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/nodes/short.res-weighted-cover-incomparability","id":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/edges/%5B%22short.res-weighted-cover-incomparability%22%2C%22step.construction_weighted_not_cover%22%2C%22supports%22%5D","kind":"supports","record_ref":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/edges/%5B%22short.res-weighted-cover-incomparability%22%2C%22step.construction_weighted_not_cover%22%2C%22supports%22%5D","semantic_class":"curated_argument_support","to":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/nodes/step.construction_weighted_not_cover"},{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/nodes/step.construction_weighted_not_cover","id":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/edges/%5B%22step.construction_weighted_not_cover%22%2C%22step.log_obstruction%22%2C%22supports%22%5D","kind":"supports","record_ref":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/edges/%5B%22step.construction_weighted_not_cover%22%2C%22step.l